cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or the WISE selection concept, please cite the paper below."
title: "WISE: Zero-Cost Connectivity within Wrench-Feasible Assignment Fibers for Heterogeneous Robot Transport"
abstract: >-
  Heterogeneous multi-robot transport couples physical task allocation with the
  communication structure needed to coordinate it. When productive utility depends on a
  low-dimensional served aggregate, the unique optimal aggregate can correspond to a
  positive-dimensional fiber of wrench-feasible compositions. A free-networkability
  modulus Gamma_E, whose positivity is necessary and sufficient for a strictly
  better-connected composition to exist anywhere on that fiber, turns a local directional
  test into a global connectivity-optimality certificate, repeated Fiedler eigenvalues
  included. WISE is the lexicographic refinement of the productive variational-equilibrium
  set computed by a semidefinite program; the spectral capacities separate zero-cost,
  costly and impossible requirements. Clearing the derived threshold gives exponential
  stability of a reduced information layer, with the same certified lower rate bound under
  a moving physical graph, and a planar closed-loop transport simulation makes the
  consequence physical. Scope: equilibrium-set geometry and centralized selection, not
  distributed Nash seeking.
